{"acceptance_length": 1, "acceptance_lengths": [], "accepted_draft_lengths": [], "benchmark": "math500", "completion": "We are given a diagram of a rectangle made up of **12 unit squares**, and we are to find the **total area of the shaded region**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the Diagram\n\nFrom the Asymptote code and the description:\n\n- The rectangle is made of **12 unit squares**, so it's a **3 by 4 rectangle** (since $3 \\times 4 = 12$).\n- The **shaded regions** are two triangles:\n  1. A **right triangle** with vertices at:  \n     - (0, 4)  \n     - (0, 0)  \n     - (2, 0)  \n  2. A **larger right triangle** with vertices at:  \n     - (0, 4)  \n     - (3, 4)  \n     - (3, 0)  \n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the Area of Each Triangle\n\n#### Triangle 1: (0, 4) \u2192 (0, 0) \u2192 (2, 0)\n\n- This is a **right triangle** with:\n  - Base = 2 units (from x = 0 to x = 2)\n  - Height = 4 units (from y = 0 to y = 4)\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}_1 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 \\times 4 = 4\n$$\n\n#### Triangle 2: (0, 4) \u2192 (3, 4) \u2192 (3, 0)\n\n- This is also a **right triangle** with:\n  - Base = 3 units (from x = 0 to x = 3)\n  - Height = 4 units (from y = 0 to y = 4)\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}_2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 \\times 4 = 6\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add the Areas\n\n$$\n\\text{Total shaded area} = \\text{Area}_1 + \\text{Area}_2 = 4 + 6 = \\boxed{10}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{10}\n$$", "draft_calls": 0, "input_ids": [151644, 872, 198, 22816, 21210, 220, 16, 553, 220, 16, 31340, 1352, 264, 22756, 11, 438, 6839, 13, 3555, 374, 279, 2790, 3082, 315, 279, 91766, 5537, 30, 508, 6405, 921, 2141, 7, 19, 6226, 1215, 2258, 2752, 2333, 258, 28357, 7, 15, 13, 22, 20, 3237, 322, 434, 4374, 19325, 198, 7559, 1188, 15, 11, 220, 19, 29621, 7, 15, 11, 220, 15, 29621, 7, 17, 11, 220, 15, 29621, 21621, 11, 17545, 7, 15, 13, 22, 20, 1106,